    section: "PRAYERS FOR COURAGE TO TAKE THE FIRST STEP",
    text: `God, I am standing at the edge of the new beginning and I cannot make myself jump. I can see where I need to go. I can feel that this is the right direction. I have prayed about it and sought counsel and done the preparation and the door is open. And I am standing at the edge, toes over the ledge, and I cannot make myself go. The jump feels too large, the landing is not visible from here, and my legs are not cooperating with my understanding that this is what I am supposed to do.

I need a push. Not a violent one — a gentle, purposeful, I-believe-in-you-enough-to-push-you push. The kind that comes through a conversation that lands at the right moment. A word from Scripture that speaks so directly to my specific situation it cannot be coincidental. A circumstance that closes the alternative options and makes the jump the only remaining reasonable choice. A peace that descends in the moment of decision that did not exist in the previous hundred moments of hesitation. Whatever the push looks like for me specifically — send it.

And in this moment — right now, in this prayer — let me experience something. A shift. A loosening of the fear that has been holding my feet at the edge. A sense of Your presence that is specifically located on the other side of the jump rather than just here at the edge with me. Let me taste something of what is on the other side of the leap that makes the leap feel worth taking. Not because I need to see the landing before I jump. But because sometimes a person just needs one more thing before they go, and I am asking for that one more thing.

Push me gently, God. I am ready to jump. I just need help with the actual jumping. In Jesus' name. Amen.`,
