    title: "God, I Have Been Preparing Long Enough — Help Me Begin",
    section: "PRAYERS FOR COURAGE TO TAKE THE FIRST STEP",
    text: `God, I have been in the preparation stage for a long time. Longer than was probably necessary. And I want to be honest about that because I think preparation has been serving double duty — as genuine readying and also as an extended form of not having to actually begin. Because as long as I am preparing, I have not yet failed. As long as I am getting ready, the dream is still perfect. As long as I am studying the water, I have not yet stepped out of the boat. The preparation has been real and also it has been long enough.

Tell me that I am ready enough to begin. Not perfectly ready — I know that is not a real category. But ready enough. Because ready enough is where all meaningful things start. The person who waits for perfect readiness never begins. The person who begins with ready enough and adjusts along the way arrives at places the waiting person never reaches. I have prepared. I have prayed. I have positioned. The preparation has been genuine. And now I am asking You to help me actually begin rather than continue preparing to begin.

Give me a beginning date. A real one. The day I stop preparing and start doing. The day the draft becomes the first version. The day the research becomes the launch. The day the prayer becomes the action. Let today be that day or let me commit to a specific day in the very near future and hold myself to it. Because the beginning that is never begun is a kind of failure too — the failure of perpetual preparation that never becomes anything. I do not want that to be my story.

Help me begin, God. I have prepared long enough. In Jesus' name. Amen.`,
