    title: "Let the Releasing Be Real and Not Just Performed",
    section: "PRAYERS FOR LETTING GO OF THE OLD TO EMBRACE THE NEW",
    text: `God, I have performed releasing before. Said the right things about letting go and moving forward and not looking back — and still been looking back while saying it. Gone through the motions of closing chapters while keeping them cracked open. Made the public declaration of moving on while privately holding onto what the declaration was supposed to have released. I know the difference between performed releasing and real releasing. And I am asking today for the real kind.

Real releasing changes something in me, not just something in my vocabulary. It is the kind where the grip actually loosens — where the obsessive thinking about what ended slows because the hold has genuinely loosened. Where the wound actually begins to close rather than staying open under a surface that has been declared healed. Where the future becomes genuinely more interesting than the past is familiar — not because I am performing that transition but because something has shifted internally that makes it true.

Do the work in me that produces real releasing rather than performed releasing. Because I cannot manufacture genuine releasing from the outside in. I can change my language and my behavior and still be in the same internal place. What I need is an internal work that is done by the right hand — Yours. The kind of releasing that happens when God reaches into the place where the thing is held and actually loosens it. I am asking for that kind. The deep kind. The kind that sticks.

Make the releasing real, God. Not just performed. Do the deep work. In Jesus' name. Amen.`,
