    text: `God, I am asking for something remarkable in this new beginning: let it introduce me to a new version of myself that I could not have met in any other way. A version that exists on the other side of what I have been through. That has depth and resilience and specific wisdom and particular ways of engaging with the world that are the direct product of the journey that brought me here. Let the new beginning be not just a new chapter in the same story — but an introduction to someone who is genuinely new.

I believe that people are genuinely changed by the seasons they go through. That the person who comes out of a hard season of starting over is not the same person who went into it. That the formation that happens in the difficult new beginning — the forced self-examination, the discovery of what you are actually made of, the encounter with God in the places where self-sufficiency is not an option — produces a version of a person that the easy seasons could not have produced. Let me be genuinely changed rather than only tested.

Let me like the new version. This matters to me because I have come through seasons that changed me in ways I did not like — that made me harder or more closed or more afraid. I am asking for the version of the change that goes the other direction. That makes me more open, more genuine, more grateful, more alive, more fully myself. That I can look in the mirror in the new season and recognize someone I am glad to be. Let the introduction to the new version of myself be a good introduction.

Let this beginning introduce me to someone worth becoming, God. In Jesus' name. Amen.`,
