    section: "PRAYERS FOR NEW IDENTITY AND SELF-DISCOVERY",
    text: `God, I have been someone else's version of me for too long. The version that someone else needed me to be. The version shaped by what was expected or what was safe or what kept the peace or what earned the approval I needed at the time. The version that was too small for what You put in me because making myself smaller was what the relationship or the environment or the role required. And I am ready to stop being that version. I am ready to find out who I actually am when I am not being shaped by external expectations.

Help me identify the specific ways I have been shrinking or performing or deferring my own genuine self. The opinions I have not expressed. The callings I have not pursued. The gifts I have kept contained. The authentic voice I have kept quieter than it should be. The personality that has been modulated to fit someone else's comfort level. The dreams that have been deferred because they were not welcome in the context I was in. Help me see the places where the real me has been suppressed — so I can begin to let her out.

Let the new beginning be a homecoming to myself. Let me rediscover what I actually enjoy, what I actually believe, what I actually want to do with the days of my life. Let the people who belong to this new chapter get the real version of me rather than a curated version. Let me stop editing myself before I open my mouth. Let me stop shrinking to fit spaces I have outgrown. Let me be the full person You made, at the full size You intended. It is time.

Help me come home to myself, God. Let the real me show up. In Jesus' name. Amen.`,
